# Service map: which repo owns what

Read this before starting any ticket. It tells you which repo(s) to touch, in which order, and how to link the work. Terms: [GLOSSARY.md](../../GLOSSARY.md).

## Ownership

| Repo | Owns | Never does |
|---|---|---|
| `{{DOCS_REPO}}` | ADRs, glossary, shared rules, agent skills, issue templates, this map | Application code, secrets, personal data |
| `<backend repo>` | Business logic, data schema and migrations, authorization enforcement, API contract | Trust client-supplied identifiers |
| `<frontend repo>` | Pages, UX, display of what the API returns | Hold secrets in public env vars, business calculations, direct database access |
| `<jobs repo>` | Async/scheduled jobs, file generation, storage | Direct database access unless an ADR allows it |

> **Contract:** `<path to API contract>` is the single source of truth for endpoints.

## Interfaces

| From → To | Transport | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| frontend → backend | HTTPS | <session / token> | |
| jobs → backend | HTTPS | <TBD — decision issue> | Do not build until decided |
| backend → database | TLS | <app role> | Never from CI or laptops against staging/prod |

## Routing table

| If the task involves… | Repos, in order |
|---|---|
| New entity / field / business rule | docs (ADR if a decision) → backend → frontend |
| New page, copy, UX only | frontend |
| New or changed endpoint | backend (contract + migration + endpoint) → consumers |
| Auth, roles, permissions | docs (ADR) → backend (`security-reviewer`) → frontend |
| Scheduled/async job, exports | docs (ADR if new resource) → backend → jobs |
| CI/CD, release workflow | affected repo(s) + docs if the release flow changes |
| Terminology | docs (`GLOSSARY.md`) |

Unsure? Use the `task-intake` skill and ask the owner.

## Cross-repo change order

1. Decision/contract first (ADR; contract agreed in the provider PR).
2. Provider (backend): migration (expand) + endpoint + contract + tests.
3. Consumers (frontend, jobs) against the merged/staged contract.
4. Docs.
5. Later release: contract migration (drop old fields) after all consumers moved.

## Linking work
- Parent issue + per-repo child issues `Part of {{ORG}}/<repo>#<n>`.
- Same branch name in every repo; each PR lists sibling PRs; merge and release in change order.

